  "notes": "Sequence transcribed from the official Program Guide PDF (Program Guide link on the official program page, anokatech.edu/programs/welding/; retrieved 2026-10-01 via the atc-website-test.azurewebsites.net staging mirror, which serves the same CMS media asset as anokatech.edu). The PDF template header prints '2023-2024'; the guide is the currently published program guide and its program name, sequence, and 66-credit total (51 technical + 15 MnTC) match the current official programs listing (Welding AAS Degree, 66 credits). The technical courses are broken out into semester-long certificates (Basic Welding Certificate, Welding Technology Diploma, Welding Fabricator Certificate) to provide quick access into a welding career. Students must earn a cumulative 2.0 GPA or higher to be eligible for graduation. This program requires students to go full-time; each semester students are required to take all courses. Some courses in this program may require a prerequisite; see course descriptions for more details. Prepares students for national certification examinations: American Society of Mechanical Engineers, American Petroleum Institute, and American Welding Society's Welding Code. CROSS-GUIDE DISCREPANCY FLAG: this AAS guide prints WELD 1209 Basic Pipe Welding as 5 credits and WELD 2000 Basic Pipe Layout as 3 credits, while the college's standalone Welding Fabricator Certificate guide (Cert 0181) prints WELD 1209 as 3 credits and WELD 2000 as 5 credits; both sources sum to 17 for the certificate block. The third-semester courses here are transcribed with the AAS guide's printed credits; the discrepancy is unresolved in the published sources and is also flagged in the inventory.",
